{"id": 22, "ts": 1780467031.736189, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s reminder that Candidate\u202fB\u2019s conscientiousness and proven stress\u2011handling give us solid evidence of operational reliability and resilience\u2014key for long\u2011haul flights. While James rightly flags the unknown numeric\u2011memory gap, we have no data indicating a deficit, so we cannot treat it as a proven risk. Before we close the discussion, I think we should also evaluate Candidate\u202fC, who demonstrates rapid, correct decision\u2011making, excellent attention skills, and a strong sense of responsibility (\u201cputs concern for others above everything\u201d). These traits directly address decision quality, attention accuracy, and responsibility\u2014areas where B\u2019s profile is less explicit. At the same time, C\u2019s difficulty communicating, perceived egocentricity, and reluctance to further education raise concerns for crew cooperation and adaptability. By comparing C\u2019s strengths and weaknesses with B\u2019s, we can confirm whether B truly remains the best overall fit. For now, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fB, but I propose we bring Candidate\u202fC into the comparison to ensure we have covered all viable options."}
