{"id": 26, "ts": 1780467074.9564166, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I agree with Emily that Candidate\u202fC brings impressive decision\u2011making speed and a flawless reliability record, and that his ability to create a positive crew atmosphere is valuable. However, the profile we have for C lacks any evidence of stress resilience or technical depth\u2014both essential for long\u2011haul operations. Moreover, his difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric reputation, and reluctance to pursue further education raise serious concerns for crew cooperation and adaptability. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB is explicitly noted as very conscientious (a clear indicator of operational reliability) and handles stress very well, directly addressing two of our highest\u2011priority criteria. His strong weather\u2011assessment skill and excellent computer abilities also cover technical competence. While B\u2019s tone issues and occasional grumpiness are noted, these are behavioral traits that can be mitigated through onboarding and coaching, and we have no concrete evidence that they would impair safety. Given the complete lack of stress\u2011handling data for C and the stronger, evidence\u2011based reliability and resilience of B, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fB."}
